---
import MockNavigation from "./MockNavigation.astro";
interface Props {
  index: number;
}
const { index } = Astro.props;
---

<div
  class="value-mockup"
  role="group"
  aria-label={`${["Model and agent setup", "Task analysis", "Model fusion"][index]} concept mockup`}
>
  <MockNavigation active={index} />
  <div class="mock-workspace">
    <header>
      <strong>
        <span class="mock-brand">niu.io</span>
        <span class="mock-location">
          {["Connections", "Task analysis", "Model fusion"][index]}
        </span>
      </strong>
      <span class="mock-status">Concept preview</span>
    </header>
    <div class="mock-body">
      {index === 0 ? (
        <>
          <h3>Your agent, connected.</h3>
          <div class="mock-box">
            <small>Agent connection</small>
            <strong>Existing agent workflow</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="mock-box tinted">
            <strong>Keep your current plan</strong>
            <p>
              Subscription access stays separate from additional paid API calls.
            </p>
          </div>
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Existing subscription</dt>
              <dd>Preferred</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>OpenRouter fallback</dt>
              <dd>Off by default</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p>
            Design goal: verified compatibility and explicit opt-in for paid
            fallback.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : index === 1 ? (
        <>
          <h3>One task. Every attempt counts.</h3>
          <p class="task-example-label">
            Prepare the narrative for a board presentation
          </p>
          <div class="cost-drivers">
            <div>
              <strong>2</strong>
              <span>iterations</span>
            </div>
            <b>→</b>
            <div>
              <strong>3 + 2</strong>
              <span>steps</span>
            </div>
            <b>→</b>
            <div>
              <strong>16k</strong>
              <span>tokens used</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="iteration-group">
            <div class="iteration-title">
              <strong>Iteration 1 · Draft</strong>
              <span>Needs revision</span>
            </div>
            <table>
              <caption class="sr-only">
                First iteration: 12,000 tokens, 3 minutes, 24 cents in model
                charges
              </caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Step</th>
                  <th>Tokens</th>
                  <th>Time</th>
                  <th>Model $</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>Research</td>
                  <td>6,000</td>
                  <td>1m 30s</td>
                  <td>$0.12</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Draft</td>
                  <td>4,000</td>
                  <td>1m</td>
                  <td>$0.08</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Review</td>
                  <td>2,000</td>
                  <td>30s</td>
                  <td>$0.04</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <div class="iteration-total">12,000 tokens · 3m · $0.24</div>
          </div>
          <div class="iteration-group">
            <div class="iteration-title">
              <strong>Iteration 2 · Repair</strong>
              <span>Accepted</span>
            </div>
            <table>
              <caption class="sr-only">
                Second iteration: 4,000 tokens, 1 minute 20 seconds, 8 cents in
                model charges
              </caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Step</th>
                  <th>Tokens</th>
                  <th>Time</th>
                  <th>Model $</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>Revise</td>
                  <td>3,000</td>
                  <td>1m</td>
                  <td>$0.06</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Review again</td>
                  <td>1,000</td>
                  <td>20s</td>
                  <td>$0.02</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <div class="iteration-total">4,000 tokens · 1m 20s · $0.08</div>
          </div>
          <div class="task-cost-total">
            <div>
              <span>Your wait</span>
              <strong>4m 20s</strong>
            </div>
            <span>+</span>
            <div>
              <span>Model spend</span>
              <strong>$0.32</strong>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>
            <strong>The repair adds 1m 20s and $0.08.</strong> Counting only the
            accepted iteration would hide the first attempt’s cost.
          </p>
          <details class="mock-cost-details">
            <summary>How to read these example costs</summary>
            <p>
              Synthetic, sequential model-only work: all five steps count. Token
              figures combine input and output; real charges depend on their
              separate rates, model and cache use. Tool, rendering, subscription
              and human-review costs are excluded. Parallel step durations
              cannot simply be added to calculate elapsed time.
            </p>
          </details>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <h3>The right balance of time and cost.</h3>
          <p>
            Combine models to meet your quality standards—within your budget and
            deadline.
          </p>
          <div
            class="comparison-scroll"
            role="region"
            aria-label="Model strategy comparison"
            tabindex="0"
          >
            <table class="comparison-matrix fusion-matrix">
              <caption class="sr-only">
                Three hypothetical strategies for the same task
              </caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Same task</th>
                  <th scope="col">
                    Expensive<small>Throughout</small>
                  </th>
                  <th scope="col">
                    Cheap<small>Throughout</small>
                  </th>
                  <th scope="col" class="matrix-selected">
                    Fusion<small>A mix of both</small>
                  </th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {[
                  ["Iterations", "1", "3", "2"],
                  ["Total steps", "3", "9", "5"],
                  ["Tokens", "12k", "36k", "21k"],
                  ["Time", "3 min", "9 min", "5 min"],
                  ["Model spend", "$1.20", "$0.36", "$0.48"],
                  ["Quality bar", "Met", "Met", "Met"],
                  ["≤ 6 min", "Pass", "Over limit", "Pass"],
                  ["≤ $0.60", "Over limit", "Pass", "Pass"],
                  ["Decision", "Fastest", "Lowest spend", "Meets both limits"],
                ].map((row, index) => (
                  <tr
                    class:list={{
                      "matrix-key": index === 3 || index === 4,
                      "matrix-decision": index === 8,
                    }}
                  >
                    <th scope="row">{row[0]}</th>
                    {row.slice(1).map((value, column) => (
                      <td class:list={{ "matrix-selected": column === 2 }}>
                        {value}
                      </td>
                    ))}
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <div class="mock-box tinted">
            <small>EXAMPLE LIMITS: ≤ 6 MIN · ≤ $0.60 · QUALITY BAR MET</small>
            <strong>Fusion meets all three.</strong>
            <p>
              It costs more than the cheap-only run, but finishes sooner. It
              costs less than the expensive-only run, while taking longer.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mock-box">
            <small>Planned strategy</small>
            <strong>
              Strong model plans → cheap model drafts → strong model reviews
            </strong>
          </div>
          <details class="mock-cost-details">
            <summary>Illustrative assumptions</summary>
            <p>
              Invented results, not measured savings. Acceptance means meeting
              the same defined quality threshold, not identical outputs. Example
              blended token rates: $0.10 per 1k for the expensive model and
              $0.01 per 1k for the cheap model. The mix uses 3k expensive tokens
              ($0.30) and 18k cheap tokens ($0.18). Real pricing separates
              input, output and cached tokens. Model spend includes every shown
              iteration; tool, subscription and human-review charges are
              excluded. Step counts include model-based checks. The time and
              quality outcomes are hypothetical, not derived from token counts.
            </p>
          </details>
        </>
      )}
    </div>
    <footer>
      Illustrative design ·{" "}
      {index > 0 ? "Synthetic data · Planned workflow" : "Planned workflow"}
    </footer>
  </div>
</div>
